\label{lem-unique-supp}
There exists a set $Y$ of points $Y_{1}<\dots <Y_{m}$, $m\le n$ such that $k-$monotone density $\hat f_{n}$ defined by a mixing probability measure $\hat G_{n}$ is the MLE if and only if $\mathop{\mathrm{supp(\hat G_{n})\subseteq Y$. In other words, any MLE
has the form:
\begin{eqnarray}
\label{mle-repres}
\hat f_{n}(x) = \sum_{j=1}^{m} a_{j}\frac{k(Y_{j}-x)_{+}^{k-1}}{Y_{j}^{k}},
\end{eqnarray}
where $a_{j}\ge 0$, $\sum a_{j}=1$ and $Y_{j}> X_{(j)}$. Moreover, the vector $(\hat f_{n}(X_{(i)}))_{i=1}^{n}$ is unique.
